// fp8 on the vector staging path.
//
// This route used to be rejected, on the grounds that fp8 was a cube *operand*
// format the bc layer implemented for GM->L1 and L1->L0A/L0B only. That was a
// statement about the registrations rather than about the hardware, and it no
// longer holds: Vector/dma.cpp registers GM<->UB and UB->L1 for both fp8
// encodings, so an fp8 tile is staged and loaded like any other element type.
//
// The registration is not quite direct. The AIV backend rejects fp8 outright --
// "type only supports pointer operations, scalar float type semantics are not
// supported" -- and the UB copy templates trip that where the cube's DMA-only
// ones do not. Each wrapper therefore keeps the fp8 name and signature that
// route resolution needs and instantiates the copy on int8_t behind a
// reinterpret_cast, which emits the same move because a copy does not read the
// element type beyond stride and layout arithmetic.
//
// What this test guards is that the route resolves at all: element types are
// shared across every copy route, so a route that can spell a name but has no
// REGISTER_* behind it fails at link time rather than as a diagnostic here.

// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/generate_mmad_ir.py fp8-vector-copy | %tla_compile - -o - 2>&1 | %filecheck %s --check-prefix=VECCOPY

// Naming the callee pins two things at once: the copy lowered rather than being
// marked illegal, and it resolved to the registered fp8 symbol rather than to
// some other element type's.
// VECCOPY: copy_gm_RowMajor_to_ub_RowMajor_fp8_e4m3fn_t
